$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General reaction procedure of Suzuki coupling
reaction on dichloromethylene derivatives (4, 13 and 26-28) with
arylboronic acids Dichloromethylene derivative (1.0 mmol), aryl-boronic
acid (2.5 mmol), Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (30 mg) and PPh3 (20 mg), potassium
carbonate (1.38 g, 10.0 mmol) and benzyltriethyl ammonium chloride (0.5
g, 2.2 mmol) were taken in a mixture of toluene (20 ml) and water (10
ml). The reaction mixture was heated at 110 ºC for 24 h in nitrogen
atmosphere. On completion of reaction the mixture was cooled, and toluene
layer was separated. On removal of toluene the product was purified by
column chromatography using dichloromethane/hexane as eluent. Preparation
of 6-(diphenylmethylene)-6H-benzo[cd]pyrene (5) According to general
reaction procedure, 6-(dichloromethylene)-6H-benzo[cd]pyrene (4) (0.32 g,
1.0 mmol) and phenylboronic acid (0.26 g, 2.5 mmol) were reacted.
Preparation of
7-(bis(4-methoxyphenyl)methylene)-3,9-di(naphthalen-2-yl)-7H-benzo[de]anthracene
(31) According to general reaction procedure,
7-(dichloromethylene)-3,9-di(naphthalen-2-yl)-7H-benzo[de]anthracene (28)
(0.55 g, 1.0 mmol) and (4-methoxyphenyl)boronic acid (0.38 g, 2.5 mmol)
were reacted. Product as yellow solid. Yield: 0.50 g, 72%. Mp: 267 °C. 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ: 8.27 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 8.10 (d, J = 8.4 Hz,
1H), 7.99 (s, 1H), 7.95-7.92 (m, 3H), 7.84-7.65 (m, 7H), 7.61 (d, J = 8.0
Hz, 1H), 7.57-7.48 (m, 4H), 7.39-7.27 (m, 5H), 7.11-7.05 (m, 3H),
6.96-6.94 (m, 2H), 6.81-6.79 (m, 2H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 3.78 (s, 3H). 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ: 158.3, 158.1, 143.4, 140.0, 138.4, 138.3, 138.2,
137.3, 136.2, 135.0, 133.7, 133.4, 133.2, 132.9, 132.7, 132.6, 132.5,
131.2, 131.1, 130.9, 130.6, 129.8, 129.1, 128.8, 128.6, 128.2, 128.1,
128.0, 127.8, 127.7, 127.6, 127.5, 127.4, 126.3, 126.1, 126.0, 125.9,
125.8, 125.4, 125.2, 124.8, 124.2, 119.4, 114.3, 114.0, 55.2, 55.1.
MALDITOF MS: calculated for [C52H36O2]+: 692.2710, found: 692.2696.
